["Define membership status from authoritative events","Document what creates, renews, lapses, suspends, or ends each membership type. Identify the official system and how payments, approved waivers, complimentary memberships, and organizational rosters reach it. The assistant may reconcile events against the rule but should not manufacture a status to make reports agree. Create an exception for unmatched payments, duplicate contacts, disputed categories, and organizations whose employee roster changed. Record effective dates so the team can explain access at the time it was granted."],
["Build the campaign from segments that matter","Separate first notices, approaching-expiry reminders, grace-period messages, lapsed outreach, organizational renewals, and cases already in discussion with staff. Suppression rules should cover completed payment, opt-out obligations where applicable, complaints, deceased contacts, and owner-directed holds. The association approves message content, timing, and audience. The assistant generates a preview count and samples records before release. A dramatic change from the expected audience should stop the send rather than become a surprise after thousands of messages."],
["Keep commercial exceptions in an owner queue","Members may ask for discounts, installment plans, retroactive access, category changes, sponsorship credit, or special treatment based on history. Provide a short intake that captures the request and supporting record, then route it to the authorized association owner. The assistant can apply a documented decision and preserve who approved it. Avoid informal chat approvals that cannot be linked to the membership record. Consistency reviews can reveal when repeated exceptions signal that the published renewal policy needs revision."],
["Constrain payment handling","Prefer approved payment pages and platform workflows rather than collecting card details through email or chat. Define what the assistant can see, resend, refund, or change. Failed payments should receive approved troubleshooting language and a secure next step; the assistant must not request sensitive authentication data. The FTC small-business cybersecurity resources provide general context, but the association must set controls that fit its processor, contracts, and legal obligations. Review exports because downloaded rosters can create unnecessary copies of personal information."],
["Reconcile benefits separately from billing","A successful payment does not guarantee that event discounts, directory listings, community access, publications, or chapter rights updated correctly. Create a post-renewal check for benefits relevant to each tier. The assistant can compare expected and observed access and route discrepancies to the system owner. It should not extend benefits simply to resolve a complaint quickly. Track which failures came from the membership source, integration delay, manual error, or unclear policy so the remedy addresses the actual cause."],
["Close the cycle with decisions, not just totals","Report eligible population, reached members, deliveries, responses, renewals, exceptions, unresolved payments, benefit failures, complaints, and staff effort with clearly defined denominators. Do not present correlation between a message and payment as certain causation. Review message fatigue and wrong-contact incidents. The renewal owner then chooses policy, segmentation, system, and staffing changes. Archive the approved campaign logic and final reconciliation so the next cycle starts from evidence instead of copying an old list."],
